INSERT INTO `astarcompo_questions` (`questionID`, `question`, `questionCategory`, `questionType`, `theme`) VALUES
(1, 'The picture below show how you lost your rabbit after a “Show-and-tell” session in school where you introduced your rabbit to your class. \r\n\r\nImagine you are the girl in the picture. \r\n\r\nWrite a letter to the residents of your neighbourhood asking them to return your rabbit to you if they see it. \r\nYou are to refer to the given pictures and information for your letter. \r\n\r\nIn your letter, include the following information: \r\n- the date you lost your rabbit \r\n- where you were when you found your rabbit was missing \r\n- two physical features of your rabbit that will help people recognise her as soon as they see her \r\n- why your rabbit is in need of care \r\n- how you can be contacted \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(2, 'On the first day of the new school year, your teacher introduced a new classmate, Alvin  Foo, who had been transferred from another class. Alvin was a notorious bully who had previously bullied you and your friends more than once.\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words about your experiences having Alvin as your classmate. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- how you felt at first when you knew Alvin was joining your class\r\n- how Alvin behaved towards you and your classmates\r\n- how you and your classmate treated Alvin\r\n- whether you tried to befriend Alvin and how you did so\r\n- whether Alvin changed his attitude or behaviour in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'School and You'),
(3, 'One evening, you were walking with a friend along the beach when you spotted a boat in the sea heading towards the shore...\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words describing what happened next. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- how you felt about the experience\r\n- who was in the boat\r\n- what they were here for\r\n- what you did when you saw the boat\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points to write an interesting and original story', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(4, 'One night, Mr Lim, a taxi driver, was driving around in his taxi when he picked up a passenger...\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- how you felt at first when you knew Alvin was joining your class\r\n- who the passenger was\r\n- what the passenger did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(5, 'Jeremy caught his classmates, Hasli, trying to make a photocopy of the examination paper for the examination they were going to have the following day...\r\n\r\nOn the first day of the new school year, your teacher introduced a new classmate, Alvin  Foo, who had been transferred from another class. Alvin was a notorious bully who had previously bullied you and your friends more than once.\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- what Jeremy did about it\r\n- how Hasli reacted\r\n- whether Jeremy was tempted to join Hasli in making a photocopy of the examination paper for himself\r\n- how things ended up\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'School and You'),
(6, 'The school bell had just rung and it was time for students to be dismissed from school. Students, eager to make their way home, rushed out of school. You were likewise about to home when you suddenly noticed a commotion at the school gate.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation and points given and drawing reference from the words and phrases given, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nSome points you can think about: \r\n-What was the commotion about? \r\n-Who were involved in the commotion? \r\n-What did the bystanders do? \r\n-What happened in the end?\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(7, 'One afternoon while he was doing his homework, David had a terrible stomachache. This was followed by diarrhoea and vomiting.\r\n\r\nOn the first day of the new school year, your teacher introduced a new classmate, Alvin  Foo, who had been transferred from another class. Alvin was a notorious bully who had previously bullied you and your friends more than once.\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- how David came to be in this state\r\n- what happened to David when he felt ill\r\n- the cause of this illness\r\n- whether it was serious\r\n- what happened to David in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(8, 'The El-lina monsoon had wreaked havoc on world weather patterns and by a freak occurrence of nature, Singapore would be having a day of snowfall for the first time in history. You have the unique opportunity of experiencing this never before phenomenon.\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words  describing what happened. You may make use of the following points:\r\n\r\n- how you felt about the experience\r\n- what you did during that day\r\n- how the snowfall affected you, your family and friends\r\n- whether you enjoyed the experience\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(9, 'You were going on a short holiday to an underdeveloped country. At the customs and immigration checkpoint, you were not allowed to enter into the country because the immigration officer claimed that your passport looked suspicious ... \r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words. You may make use of the following points: \r\n\r\n- the events leading up to the situation described \r\n- what was wrong with your passport whether you were allowed into the country in the end \r\n- If yes, why were you finally allowed to enter?\r\n- If not, what did you do? \r\n\r\nYou may also make use of your own ideas to include other relevant points to write an interesting and original story. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Overseas Trip'),
(10, 'I could not believe what I was seeing. Chaotic thoughts raced through my mind and my legs were trembling ...\r\n\r\nUsing the sentences given above in any part of your composition, write a story of at least 150 words describing what happened. You may make use of the following points: \r\n\r\n- the events leading up to the situation described \r\n- what caused you to end up in that state \r\n- what happened to you in the end \r\n\r\nYou may also make use of your own ideas to include other relevant points to write an interesting and original story. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(11, 'As you and your father were approaching your lift lobby, you saw a man push your elderly neighbour into the lift. Before you could find out what was happening, the lift doors  closed.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story:\r\n- what went through your mind\r\n- what you and your father did next\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Humour'),
(12, 'You were waiting for your mother outside a shop in a shopping mall when you heard a strange noise. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story: \r\n- what cause the noise\r\n- what happened next\r\n- how it all ended\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(13, 'You and your friends were at a bus stop when you noticed an elderly woman walking in an unsteady manner towards you.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story: \r\n- what happened to the elderly woman\r\n- what you and your friends did next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(14, 'You were walking towards a shop. Suddenly, you saw people running out of the shop.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story: \r\n- why the people were running out of the shop\r\n- what you did next\r\n- how it all ended \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(15, 'You were in a library when you heard an unusual sound tat grew louder and louder.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story: \r\n- what the us usual sound was\r\n- what you did next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(16, 'It is now Friday evening and the end of a busy week for you\r\n\r\nWrite an email to your best friend, Tom, telling him of the busy week you have had and your plans for the weekend.\r\n\r\nYou Should refer to your weekly planner below.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(17, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below:\r\n- why the man was in a hurry\r\n- what the two boys were doing\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(18, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou must make use of the points below in your story:\r\n- why the children were under the table\r\n- what happened next\r\n- how it all ended\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Celebrations'),
(19, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nYou must make use of the points below in your story: \r\n- what the woman was doing and why \r\n- what happened next \r\n- how it all ended \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Celebrations'),
(20, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nYou must make use of the points below in your story: \r\n- what happened to the man with the camera\r\n- what happened next \r\n- how it all ended \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(21, 'One evening, as you were walking home, you heard footsteps behind you. You turned around to see who or what was behind you. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below:\r\n- who the footsteps belonged to \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Humour'),
(22, 'It was a Sunday afternoon. You and your family were relaxing in the living room when the doorbell rang. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who rang the doorbell \r\n- what you and your family did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(23, 'Once you were treated unfairly by someone in your family. You were blamed for something that was not actually your fault. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what you were blamed for, and why \r\n- how you felt and what you did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(24, 'I was having a difficult time making up my mind. I looked around me. No one was looking. I decided to take the small parcel lying on the ground. Suddenly, a man grabbed my arm. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n  \r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who that man was \r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(25, 'You were swimming with your friends at a swimming pool. All of a sudden you saw something big flying towards the pool. Then you heard a loud splash. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below:\r\n- what the flying object was \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(26, 'One day you were at an MRT station. As you were about to board the train, you heard someone calling your name. You turned to look behind. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who was calling your name \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(27, 'As you were taking a stroll in the park one evening, a small child approached you. The child was crying. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the child was crying \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(28, 'One afternoon, you were relaxing in your room, when all of a sudden, you heard a loud crash followed by a scream coming from the living room. You rushed outside to see what had happened. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what caused the loud crash \r\n- who screamed \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(29, 'As you were walking along a quiet street, you heard a rustling noise coming from the bushes behind you. You decide to investigate. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n \r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what was making the noise \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(30, 'You were sitting for a test in school. Suddenly, a teacher entered your classroom. She/He was in a great panic.\r\n \r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the teacher was panic-stricken \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(31, 'Your mother told you to look after your brother while she shopped in a crowded market area. However, you were distracted by something and did not notice your brother walk away. You searched frantically for him. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what you were distracted by \r\n- how you felt when you realized that your brother was gone \r\n- what happened in the end\r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(32, 'One evening, you were watching television at home when you smelled smoke. Suddenly you heard your neighbour shouting for help. You ran to help.\r\n \r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below \r\n- where the smoke was coming from \r\n- how you felt and what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(33, 'You were just about to take a shower when the phone rang. In an urgent voice, the caller asked you to meet him/her in till neighbourhood park immediately. You rush to the park. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who the caller was \r\n- what the caller wanted \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(34, 'One afternoon, you received a parcel addressed to you. Feeling very excited, you quickly unwrapped it. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what was in the parcel - who it was from \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(35, 'You were celebrating your birthday party when the doorbell rang. You ran to open the door. There was an unexpected visitor at the door.\r\n \r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who the unexpected visitor was \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(36, 'You and your family were relaxing at a beach, when all of a sudden, you saw some people running in different directions.\r\n \r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the people were running \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(37, 'One afternoon, you returned home from school. You saw two men standing in front of your neighbour''s flat. One of them was struggling with the door. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n \r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who the two men were \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(38, 'Once, you pleaded with your sibling to lend you something that was very precious to him/her. He/She finally agreed. Then, before you could return it, you lost it. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what it was that you wanted to borrow \r\n- how you lost it \r\n- what you did You may reorder the points. \r\n\r\nYou may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(39, 'One day, as you were doing your homework, your mother sat down next to you. She said that she had something important to tell you. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what your mother told you \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(40, 'One of your classmates was very unfriendly towards the other pupils. Because of this, the other pupils did not like to talk to her/him. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.  \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what she/he did that seemed unfriendly \r\n- how you tried to be her/his friend \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'School and You'),
(41, 'Write a story based on the picture below.\r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below:\r\n- why the boys were fighting\r\n- what the others did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
