(56, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what the girl with the pony tail was doing\r\n- what the boy in the striped shirt did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Celebrations'),
(57, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the pot fell\r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(58, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the two boys were running away\r\n- what the others did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(59, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the girl was upset\r\n- what the others did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(60, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- who the party was for\r\n- what the boys were doing\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Celebrations'),
(61, 'Study the pictures below carefully.\r\n\r\nImagine you are the girl in the pictures. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to the Manager of Bedok Public Library to inform him of the librarian''s good deed.\r\n\r\nYou are to refer to the given pictures and details for your email. \r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following information: \r\n- when you were at the library\r\n- the name of the librarian on duty\r\n- what you discovered at the bus stop\r\n- how the librarian helped you\r\n- why you could not thank her\r\n- why you feel thankful to the librarian\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(62, 'During recess, you and your friends discussed what birthday gift to buy for Sally.\r\nYou took notes during the discussion. Study the pictures below carefully.\r\nImagine you are Ben.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to Roy to tell him of the choice of the gift.\r\n\r\nYou are to refer to the given information for your email. \r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following information: \r\n- what you and your friends decided to buy for Sally\r\n- why Sally would find the gift useful\r\n- who disagreed to buying a watch and why \r\n- why Devi thought a purse was not a good idea\r\n- how you and your friends would not make the gift special\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(63, 'Your school library will be organising a library festival. Shown below is an information sheet on the event with some notes you have made on it.\r\n\r\nYour classmate, Chris, has been unwell and will be away from school for a few more days. Chris has not seen the information sheet yet.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to inform Chris about the event. \r\n\r\nYou are to refer to the given information.\r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following information:\r\n- the name of the event\r\n- what Primary Six pupils need to do to take part in the event\r\n- the venue for ''Write a story competition'' and what to bring for the activity\r\n- one activity which both of you are likely to take part in and why\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(64, 'The pictures below show what Amy Tay did after she saw what happened to a boy in school.\r\n\r\nImagine you saw what happened in the pictures.\r\n\r\nWrite a letter to your Principal, Mr Raj, requesting him to include in the assembly talk what Amy Tay did.\r\n\r\nYou are to refer to the given information for your letter.\r\n\r\nIn your letter, include the following information:\r\n- the date you saw what happened\r\n- what Amy told the boy not to do, and why\r\n- what Amy immediately did for the boy\r\n- the advice Amy gave the boy about his worksheet\r\n- one important value that pupils can learn from Amy\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(65, 'Study the pictures below carefully. \r\nImagine you are Mary, the president of the club.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to Mrs Choo to request her help.\r\n\r\nYou are to refer to the given information for your email.\r\n\r\nIn your email. include the following information:\r\n- which club you belong to\r\n- the purpose of the camp\r\n- when and where the camp will be held\r\n- what specific help you need from Mrs Choo\r\n- when Mrs Choo need to reply to you\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(66, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou must make uses of the points below in your story:\r\n- what happened to the boy in striped T-shirt\r\n- what the other people did next\r\n- how it all ended\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(67, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nYou must make uses of the points below in your story: \r\n- what happened to the boy wearing the cap \r\n- what the other people did next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(68, 'Your teacher gave you a flyer shown below, advertsing an enrichment programme to be conducted  during the school holidays and encouraged to sign up for it.\r\n\r\nYou are planning to sign up for the programme and wish to invite your friend from another school, Ravi, who is of the same age as you, to join in as well. You believe that the programme will help him to improve in his studies. Write an email to Ravi to ask him if he would like to enrol for the programme. \r\n\r\nYou should include the following points in your email: \r\n\r\n- what the programme is about \r\n- the benefits of joining the programme \r\n- why you want him to join the programme\r\n- where and when the programme will be held \r\n- how much he must pay to attend the programme\r\n- how to register and pay for the programme \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You must write in complete sentences. ', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(69, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nYou must make use of the points below in your story:\r\n- what happened to the man near the staircase\r\n- what happened next\r\n- how it all ended \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(70, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what the children are doing \r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(71, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what happened before this\r\n- what the children were doing\r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(72, 'One day, you and your sibling were strolling in a nearby park. Suddenly, you heard a noise coming from behind you.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below:\r\n- how you and your sibiling felt\r\n- what the both of you did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(73, 'You were walking towards the staffroom when you caught your friend quietly sobbing in a corner.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why your friend was sobbing\r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(74, 'You were at the pool. All of a sudden, you saw something big flying towards the pool. Then you heard a loud splash.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nIn your story, make use of the points below. \r\n- What the flying saucer was\r\n- What happened next\r\n- What happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points and may include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Humour'),
(75, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what did the dog found\r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the point. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(76, 'You were in a shopping mall when you heard a loud noise...\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a story of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nYou must make use go the points below in your story: \r\n- what made the loud noise\r\n- what happened next\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(77, 'Write a story based on the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor your story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what the two boys are doing\r\n- what the others did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the point. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(78, 'Write a story based on the situation in the picture below. \r\nYour story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou must make use of the points below in your story:\r\n- what happened to one of the boys\r\n- how the other boys felt and what they did\r\n- what happened in the end', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(79, 'Police Report – Witness At an Accident Scene\r\n\r\nYou have jut witnessed an accident along a major road near your home. Write a report about what you have seen to submit to the police. In your report, include the following points:\r\n\r\n-	the time of the accident\r\n-	where the accident happened\r\n-	what you were doing at the time\r\n-	how the accident happened\r\n-	what you did / how you reacted\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(80, 'Police Report – Witness At A Crime Scene\r\n\r\nYou were shopping with a friend at the busy HDB Hub. There, you witnessed a crime in action. \r\n\r\nWrite a police report about what you saw. \r\n\r\nIn your report, include the following points:\r\n-	the time of day\r\n-	who you were with\r\n-	what you were doing at the time\r\n-	what you saw\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(81, 'Below is an article from a newspaper.\r\n\r\nYour friend lives in the area where the flood occurred. \r\nWrite an email to enquire about your friend and tell your friend what you have found out from the article. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the article.\r\nInclude the following information in your email:\r\n\r\n- What happened to your friend''s house\r\n- how many people are affected\r\n- how your friend;s life has changed\r\n- what your friend and her family plan to do\r\n- how you intend to help your friend \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(82, 'Police Report – Stolen Properties\r\n\r\nImagine you were at a busy shopping area yesterday. The following shows what happened while you were there. \r\n\r\nWrite a report for submission to the Police about your missing mobile phone. \r\nIn your report, indicate:\r\n-	where you have been\r\n-	the time of day\r\n-	what you did with the phone\r\n-	when you last saw the phone\r\n-	when you discovered the phone was missing\r\n-	what else you have discovered\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(83, 'Police Report – Lost Property\r\n\r\nImagine you are making a police report on your lost wallet the next day. Use the pictures below to help you write your report. In your report, indicate:\r\n-	where you were (going)\r\n-	the time of day\r\n-	what bus you took\r\n-	where you alighted\r\n-	when you discovered the loss\r\n-	what you had in your wallet\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(84, 'Sales Report\r\n\r\nYour school has just had a one-day flea market to raise funds for a new extension. Together with a few of your classmates, you were placed in charge of a stall selling several food items. You are required to report on the sales of the items and make recommendations for the next fund-raising event. The following is a compilation of the sales figures you have recorded during the flea market. Make use of it to write a sales report for submission to your teacher.\r\n\r\nIn your report, include:\r\n-	the kinds of items you sold at the stall\r\n-	the cost and sales price of each item\r\n-	the amount of money you collected for each item\r\n-	the profit (or loss) made for each item\r\n-	your conclusion and recommendations', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(85, 'Your Science teacher, Mrs Lim is about to start an enrichment class for the students in your level. Imagine that you are Kelly, the Science Representative for your class, and that you have been asked by Mrs Lim to help do a review on some new assessment books in the market, for the purpose of choosing one for use during the enrichment class. Below are the notes you have taken as you go through the books. \r\n\r\nWrite a report to your teacher on your review. \r\n\r\nIn your report, include: \r\n- the titles of the books you were reviewing\r\n- the price of the books\r\n- your feeling about the books\r\n- your conclusion and recommendation', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(86, 'Imagine that you are Carol. You have been assigned to do a Science experiment with three other friends, Jaclyn, Joseph and Kane. The following is a chart your group members have drawn up based on the results of the experiment.\r\n\r\nObjective:\r\nTo find out if plants lose water through their leaves\r\n\r\nMaterials:\r\n2 clear plastic bags, sticky tape, a growing plants, plastic plate, timer\r\n\r\nMethod:\r\n1.	Tape a clear plastic bag around some leaves of a growing plant. Make sure the bag is closed tight. Leave the plant in the sun.\r\n2.	Fill the other plastic bag with air and close it tight, then tape it to the plastic plate to keep it from flying away. Put the plate and bag next to the plant.\r\n\r\nBelow is the Observation chart.\r\n\r\nOther observations:\r\n1.	The bag of air remained unchanged throughout the experiment.\r\n2.	The bag around the leaves got foggier and foggier as time passed. The droplets of water in the bag also became bigger and bigger.\r\n3.	The leaves inside the bag were wet with water. The other leaves were dry.\r\n\r\nWrite a report for your Science teacher, Mr Soon, based on your observations. In your report, include the following:\r\n\r\n-	what your experiment was about\r\n-	the materials you used\r\n-	how the experiment was done\r\n-	how often you made the observations\r\n-	your observations\r\n-	your conclusion', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(87, 'Book Review\r\n\r\nYour teacher requires you to write a review about a book that you have read during the school holidays. You have just read the book from ‘The Chronicles of Narnia’ = ‘The Lion, The Witch And The Wardrobe’ written by C.S. Lewis, and decide to write a review on it. The following are some notes you have jotted down about the book. Use them to write your review. In your review, include the following points:\r\n-	who wrote the story\r\n-	what the story is about\r\n-	what you have learnt from the story\r\n-	what you like/dislike about the story\r\n-	whether you would recommend it to anyone else.\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Review', 'Situational', ''),
(88, 'Summary\r\n\r\nBelow is a passage you have just read. You find it interesting and wish to share it with your brother. Unfortunately, he is too busy to read it. Write a summary of the passage in a maximum of 100 words, so that your brother can read it and understand your concerns.', 'Summary', 'Situational', ''),
(89, 'Advertisement For The Notice Board\r\n\r\nYour mother has a portable Chillo air-conditioner that is almost as good as new. It has dimensions of 914mm X 508mm X 419mm and a power of 18000 BTU. It comes with a remote control and is fairly easy to operate. After buying it, she finds that the family does not need it after all. As it has been almost a year since she purchased it, she has decided to sell it off at 30% discount off the price she paid for it (S900). As she is very busy, she has asked you to help her write an advertisement to post on the common notice board of your flat.  Below is her business card.\r\n\r\nIn your advertisement, include:\r\n-	the caption\r\n-	a catchy phrase or sentence to attract attention\r\n-	a short description of the air-conditioner\r\n-	the price\r\n-	the person to contact\r\n-	the contact number', 'Advertisement', 'Situational', ''),
(90, 'Advertisement For the Newspapers\r\n\r\nBelow is an Advertisement taken from a newspaper.\r\n\r\nImagine that you are Jason. Write an advertisement to sell your puppies, for posting in the newspapers. In your advertisement, include:\r\n-	the caption\r\n-	a catchy phrase or sentence to attract attention\r\n-	a short description of the puppies\r\n-	the price\r\n-	your name and telephone number.\r\n', 'Advertisement', 'Situational', ''),
(91, 'Notice – Lost Pet\r\n\r\nYour faithful dog, Lulu, a white fluffy Maltese, has gone missing. You have searched for two days and are getting desperate. You decide to put up a “Lost Pet” notice. Below is a page from your diary.\r\n', 'Notice', 'Situational', ''),
(92, 'Below is a brochure from the Singapore Zoo.\r\n\r\nYou want to celebrate your birthday at the zoo.\r\nWrite an email to enquire more about having a party at the zoo.\r\n\r\nYou should refer to the brochure.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email:\r\n\r\n- which part of the zoo can the party be held at\r\n- if there is a discount for larger groups\r\n- where the food is catered from\r\n- if adults need to be present at the party\r\n- what is in the gift bags\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(93, 'Announcement\r\n\r\nImagine you are working at the information counter of a big shopping mall. Currently, the mall is having a 3-day ‘free gift’ promotion (from 20 Feb to 22 Feb) in which every shopper who produces a receipt for more than $50 purchase at the mall gets a free designer mug. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the response has been overwhelming and you have run out the mugs within a day. Below is a memo you have just received from the mall’s management.\r\n\r\nDue to a bout of flu, you have lost your voice and are unable to make the announcement. Write out the announcement for your part-time helper. In the announcement, include:\r\n-	what happened to the designer mugs\r\n-	what the shoppers can do (when and how) to redeem their mugs\r\n-	how the Management feels about the arrangement\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Announcement', 'Situational', ''),
(94, 'Notice\r\n\r\nImagine you are the manager of the ‘Towering Heights’ condominium. Following a consensus during the last Annual General Meeting on 31 July 2008, you have arranged to have all the common water pipes changed. Below is the schedule you have worked out with the contractor, Beta Water Pte Ltd.\r\n\r\nAs advised by the contractor, the water supply to the affected blocks will be cut off at the schedule time. Residents of the affected blocks will have to store enough water for their use before the work on the pipe replacement begins.\r\n\r\nWrite a notice to post on the common notice board of the condominium. \r\n\r\nIn your notice, include:\r\n-	the reason for the cessation of water supply\r\n-	the blocks affected and the dates and time for the works\r\n-	what the residents have to do\r\n-	how the management feels about the inconvenience caused to the residents\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Notice', 'Situational', ''),
(95, 'Instructions – Chores\r\n\r\nYour mother has just employed a new foreign domestic helper. She is from the village and has never operated any modern machinery in her life. Now, she is nervous about having to operate the various machines in your home. On top of that, she is worried that she will forget what things she has to prepare for you because of certain special requirements based on your school schedule. \r\n\r\nDraw up an instruction sheet to help her remember what she has to do on which day.\r\n', 'Instruction', 'Situational', '');
INSERT INTO `astarcompo_questions` (`questionID`, `question`, `questionCategory`, `questionType`, `theme`) VALUES
(96, 'Instructions – Job\r\n\r\nImagine that you are working as a customer service officer at a big toy shop. You have to go on urgent leave the next day but need to get some things done. Below are some notes you have taken down about your duties for the next day:\r\n\r\nLeave a note for the officer covering your duties, Louise, to instruct her about the things to do while you are absent. ', 'Note', 'Situational', ''),
(97, 'Instructions – Manual\r\n\r\nBelow is a page from the instruction manual for a washing machine.\r\n\r\nIt is too complicated for Tessie, the new foreign domestic worker that your mother has just employed. Simplify it and write a new set of instructions for her so that she can understand how to operate the washing machine more easily.\r\n', 'Instruction', 'Situational', ''),
(98, 'Letter – Instructions\r\n\r\nImagine you have just shifted to a new apartment. Below is your address.\r\n\r\nCurrently, you are subscribing to a magazine, ‘Kidophrenia’. Your subscriptions number is KP-331. You need to inform the magazine distributor (Mega-Zeens Pte Ltd) to direct the magazine to your new house. Moreover, because you are going to migrate to America in Jan 2009, you need to stop your subscription after the December issue. As you have already paid for the subscription up to June 2009, you need to obtain a refund from the magazine distributor. \r\n\r\nWrite a letter to the Director (Customer Service) of the magazine distributor with your instructions. In your letter, indicate:\r\n-	where to direct the magazines to\r\n-	when to send the magazines to a new place\r\n-	your reason for terminating the subscription early\r\n-	when to stop the magazines subscription\r\n-	what you expect from the magazine distributor\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(99, 'Below is an advertisement at a community club. \r\n\r\nYou find the course very interesting. \r\nWrite an email enquiring more about the course. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the advertisement. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n\r\n- what the class size is \r\n- how to sign up for a trial lesson \r\n- differences and similarities with other Math courses\r\n- when the lessons will be held \r\n- how the lessons are taught \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. Remember to write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(100, 'Letter to the Press – Complaint\r\n\r\nLately, your housing estate has become very hot. The trees that used to line the street have been chopped down after complaints by some neighbours about the noise caused by some roosting crows. Unfortunately, the chopping down of the trees not only did not solve the problem, as the crows have decided to settle on the rooftops, but also gave rise to some other problems, like the damage to the scenery, the unbearable heat and the dirtying of the rooftops by the crows’ dropping. You wish the authorities will spare a thought for the environment and replant the trees while getting rid of the crows by some other means.\r\n\r\nWrite a letter of complaint to the press to express your displeasure at what has happened. In your letter, indicate:\r\n-	the original problem\r\n-	what action was taken to solve the problem\r\n-	what new problems have arisen\r\n-	what you expect to be done\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(102, 'You were rollerblading near the lift lobby of your block of flats when you noticed a brown haversack next to one of the lifts. You went closer and realised that there was something sharp inside the bag.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. In your composition, make use of the points below:\r\n\r\n- what you did next\r\n- how you felt\r\n- what happened in the end', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(104, 'Read the cinema advertisement below.\r\n\r\nYour mother has offered to take you and  a friend to the cinema this weekend.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to a friend inviting him or her to come with you to see one of the films.\r\n\r\nRefer to the cinema advertisement when writing your email.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email:\r\n- your mother''s offer\r\n- the films featured in the advertisement\r\n- which film you want to see and why\r\n- information about time and place\r\n- arrangements for meeting and travelling to the cinema\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(105, 'Read the flyer below.\r\n\r\nYou and your family are going to the Blue Lagoon Water Park on Saturday, 22 May in the afternoon, from 1.30pm - 6pm. Your parents have said you can invite a friend to come with you.\r\n\r\nWrite an email inviting your friend Jack to spend the afternoon with you.\r\n\r\nRefer to the flyer when writing your email.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your invitation:\r\n- why Jack should come with you\r\n- name of the water park, date and time to meet\r\n- attractions of the water park\r\n- some safety aspects of the park\r\n- address of the website to find out more about the water park\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(106, 'Look at the birthday card below.\r\n\r\nYour grandparents have sent you a birthday card with pictures of four presents.\r\n\r\nWrite a letter to them saying which present you would like.\r\n\r\nRefer to the card when writing your letter.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter.\r\n- your thanks\r\n- which present you prefer and why\r\n- enquiries about your grandparents'' health\r\n- information about your family\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(107, 'Look at the programme and the notes below.\r\n\r\nYour school organised a visit to the Science Museum last Friday.\r\n\r\nWrite a report of the visit.\r\n\r\nRefer to the programme and the notes.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your report.\r\n- when you visited the museum\r\n- what you did at the museum\r\n- the different topics you learnt about\r\n- why you enjoyed the day\r\n- how you felt about the different activities\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(108, 'Look at the advertisement below.\r\n\r\nYou want to do some of the activities described in the advertisement and want a friend to come with you.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to your best friend, Tim, to suggest that he join you on a Saturday Adventure.\r\n\r\nRefer to the advertisement when writing your email.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email.\r\n- the activities you want to do and why\r\n- why you want your friend to come\r\n- ask what activities your friend wants to do\r\n- what other activities your friend wants to do\r\n- what other information you need to find out\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(109, 'Look at the advertisement below.\r\n\r\nYou have been staying at the Seahorse Family Resort with your parents and younger brother for a wonderful week''s holiday. You and your younger brother, Mark, have been swimming in the sea and in the pools, and have been joining in classes in one of the offered sports or leisure activities.\r\n\r\nWrite a postcard to your grandparents, explaining how you have spending your holiday.\r\n\r\nRefer to the advertisement when writing your postcard.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information when writing your postcard.\r\n- a description of the resort\r\n- the accommodation\r\n- the activities you have been doing\r\n- how much you enjoying yourself\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Postcard', 'Situational', ''),
(110, 'Look at the notice below.\r\n\r\nYou want to participate in the sponsored swim and raise $50.\r\n\r\nWrite and email to your aunt asking her to sponsor you.Refer to the notice when writing your email.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email:\r\n- information about the event\r\n- who is sponsoring the event\r\n- why ''Link the World'' should be supported\r\n- how many laps you may swim\r\n- how much money you want to raise\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(111, 'Look at the flyer below.\r\n\r\nYou are a member of Eastbay Primary School Geography Club and would like to attend the talk on ''Crossing Greenland''. You wish to interview Ms Henderson about her trip and write an article for the school newsletter. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to Ms Henderson asking if it would be possible to ask her a few questions after her talk.\r\n\r\nRefer to the flyer when writing your email.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email:\r\n- why you want to interview Ms Henderson\r\n- what the best and worst moments of your trip were\r\n- what other details you wish to obtain from Ms Henderson\r\n- other aspects of the trip you are particularly interested in\r\n- if you can use some of her photos for your article\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.\r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(112, 'Look at the diary below.\r\n\r\nIt is Friday evening and you have had a wonderful five days.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to a friend telling him or her what you have been doing\r\n\r\nRefer to the diary when writing your email.\r\n\r\nIncude the following information in your email:\r\n- your arrival\r\n- the volleyball match\r\n- the local area\r\n- windsurfing\r\n- how you feel\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(113, 'Look at the announcement below.\r\n\r\nYou and your family are attending the school concert. You would like to bring a friend.\r\n\r\nWrite a letter to a friend inviting him or her to the concert.\r\n\r\nRefer to the announcement when writing your letter.\r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter:\r\n- what the occasion is\r\n- why you want your friend to come\r\n- time and place\r\n- arrangements for going to the concert\r\n- when your friend should decide\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(114, 'Look at the advertisement below.\r\n\r\nYour parents organised a birthday party for you and your friends on 6 June at Billy''s Burger Restaurant. Unfortunately, the party was very disappointing. \r\n\r\nWrite a letter of complaint to the manager of the restaurant. \r\n\r\nRefer to the advertisement in your letter. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter: \r\n- guests were divided into two tables of six and one table of two \r\n- there was no salad with the meal \r\n- only one party game was organised \r\n- play area was closed for renovation, guests had nothing to do before the meal \r\n- ''gift'' was a plastic toy car, unsuitable for 12 year-olds \r\n- date of the party\r\n- request for a refund of some of the price your parents paid \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(115, 'Look at the email below.\r\n\r\nYou would like to go to the circus school with your friend. \r\n\r\nWrite to Tom accepting his invitation. \r\n\r\nRefer to the email and advertisement when writing your letter. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter: \r\n- a thank-you for the invitation \r\n- what you would like to do and why \r\n- questions about Tom''s choice of activities \r\n- asking for more information (when, where, cost etc.) \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(116, 'Look at the publicity material below.\r\n\r\nYou would like to attend the Music Summer School but need more information\r\n\r\nWrite an email to Miss Sing. \r\n\r\nRefer to the publicity material when writing your email. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- you play the violin (five years experience, intermediate level) and the piano (recently started), is instruction in two instruments possible? \r\n- you recently had a small operation and cannot swim for months. Is there another sport you could do? \r\n- ask for more information about accommodation. Are the rooms shared? How many children per room? \r\n- Is vegetarian food available? \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(117, 'Look at the programme below.\r\n\r\nYou would like to enrol in two after-school activities. You would prefer to do them with a friend. \r\n\r\nWrite to a friend to persuade him or her to enrol with you. \r\n\r\nRefer to the programme when writing your letter. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter: \r\n- your choice of activities \r\n- reasons for choice \r\n- description / explanation of activities \r\n- time of activities \r\n- why your friend should come \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(118, 'Look at the flyer below.\r\n\r\nYou want to invite a friend to go to the City Zoo open day with you. \r\n\r\nWrite an email inviting your friend. \r\n\r\nRefer to the flyer in your invitation. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- why you want to go \r\n- why you want your friend to go \r\n- date, times and cost of open day \r\n- some of the activities available \r\n- which activities you would like to do \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(119, 'Look at the programme below.\r\n\r\nA penfriend is visiting your city for the first time. You have planned a day out. \r\n\r\nWrite an email describing your plans for your day out together. \r\n\r\nRefer to the programme when writing your email. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- how you will travel in the city \r\n- things you like in the museum \r\n- animals you like in the zoo \r\n- your penfriend''s opinion \r\n- leaving the city \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(120, 'Look at the flyer below.\r\n\r\nYou would like to volunteer to take care of someone''s pet as part of your Community Service duty for your scout''s badge. \r\n\r\nWrite an email offering your services.\r\n\r\nRefer to the flyer when writing the email. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- you have a dog at home and walk it daily \r\n- your parents agree to let you volunteer \r\n- why you want to volunteer \r\n- you are free for one hour on Wednesday and Saturday afternoons \r\n- you have already done some community service, picking up litter \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(121, 'Look at the email and programme below.\r\n\r\nYour friend Helen has invited you to join her for some beach activities.\r\n\r\nWrite a letter accepting the invitation. \r\n\r\nRefer to the programme and email when writing  your letter. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your letter: \r\n- thanks for and acceptance of the invitation \r\n- how well you can swim \r\n- your two choices of activities \r\n- the reasons for your choice \r\n- inquiries about Helen''s wishes \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(122, 'Look at the webpage below.\r\n\r\nYou are interested in subscribing to Kids'' Crafts and Activities but would some more information. \r\n\r\nWrite an email asking for more details. \r\n\r\nRefer to the webpage in your email. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- if you change your mind and wish to unsubscribe, are you entitled to a refund? \r\n- how many activities are available each month, always the same number? \r\n- are ideas for all categories (food fun, science projects etc) included every month? \r\n- are all the activities available to every subscriber, or does it depend on the age of the subscriber? \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(123, 'Look at the announcement below.\r\n\r\nYou wish to invite a friend to Come to the Carnival with you. Write an invitation to your friend. \r\n\r\nRefer to the programme when writing your invitation. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your invitation: \r\n- date and time of the carnival \r\n- the main events \r\n- your suggestions for afternoon activities \r\n- what ''Hands Across the Ages'' is \r\n- how your friend can get further information \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(124, 'Look at the recipe below.\r\n\r\nYour best friend came to lunch and you made an omelette. Your friend thought it was delicious.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to your friend and include instructions for making the omelette. \r\n\r\nRefer to the recipe when writing your email. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n\r\n- why you are sending the recipe \r\n- the secret of making the omelette light \r\n- how much seasoning to use \r\n- why the cooking time is important \r\n- how to present the dish \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(125, 'Look at the map and notes below.\r\n\r\nYou went on a school visit to the zoo. You made notes on what you saw. \r\n\r\nWrite a report on your visit. \r\n\r\nRefer to the map and notes when writing your report. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your report: \r\n- date and venue of the trip \r\n- what you saw in the monkey house \r\n- how you felt in the reptile house \r\n- your reactions to the lions and elephants \r\n- the best thing about the visit \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(126, 'Look at the handout and notes below.\r\n\r\nYour parents took you and your younger sister (aged eight) to see the play ''MuIan'' last Saturday. \r\n\r\nWrite an review of the play. \r\n\r\nRefer to the handout and your notes on the play in your review. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your review \r\n- which book / film the play was based on \r\n- what the theatre was like \r\n- the story of the play \r\n- what you thought of the character of Mulan \r\n- why you recommend the play \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. ', 'Review', 'Situational', ''),
(127, 'Look at the poster below.\r\n\r\nYou and your friend are interested in mountain climbing. \r\n\r\nWrite an email inviting your friend to the Cinema. \r\n\r\nRefer to the poster in your invitation. \r\n\r\nInclude the following information in your email: \r\n- film only showing for one night, on weekday in school term \r\n- which aspects of the film should interest you both \r\n- reserve to make sure you can get seats \r\n- need to get parents'' permission first will need to do homework before going out \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(128, 'Look at the flyer below.\r\n\r\nYou want to do the 10km fun run because you like running and think that the charity is a very good cause. You need sponsors to raise as much money as charity possible. You have already started training by attending the training sessions on a Wednesday afternoon. \r\n\r\nWrite a letter to your aunt, asking her to sponsor you. \r\n\r\nRefer to the flyer when writing your letter. \r\n\r\nIn your letter include the following points: \r\n- why you want to do the race \r\n- how you are preparing \r\n- what the money will be used for \r\n- an invitation to watch the race \r\n- the date and time of the race \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(129, 'You had arranged to meet a friend to play in the park at 4 o''clock one afternoon. By 5 o''clock your friend had still not arrived. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(130, 'You were a little late for school and got off the bus in a hurry. When you arrived at school, you realised that you had left your school bag on the bus. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you realised you had left your bag on the bus \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(131, 'Your friend had invited you to a beach barbecue one Saturday lunchtime. when you arrived, there was nobody there. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(132, 'You decided to do agood turn for your neighbour and clean out his bird cage. As you opened the cage, the bird flew out of the cage and perched on the open window sill. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you saw the bird on the window sill \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(133, 'You were walking down the street with your mother when you saw a man in front of you snatch the bag of an elderly woman and run off down the street.\r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- what you saw\r\n- what happened next\r\n- how it all ended \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(134, 'It was your mother''s birthday and you decided to make her a cake. While cake was baking, your friend phoned you and you forgot about the cake. The cake burnt badly and the kitchen smelled of burnt food. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you realised the cake was burnt \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(135, 'I was looking out of my bedroom window one night when I noticed a strange object in the sky. It was brightly lit and appeared to be getting closer. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- what you saw \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(136, 'You were cycling through the park when you noticed up ahead of you a child lying on the ground, crying. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you saw the crying child \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(137, 'Your friend lent you a DVD a few weeks ago and you enjoyed it very much. Yesterday, your friend asked for the DVD back but, when you looked, you could not find it anywhere. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points inyour composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points, You may also include other relevantpoints. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(138, 'Your mother had given you some money to buy your little sister an ice cream and something for yourself. You bought your sister the ice cream and had decided to buy yourself a magazine. Just as you left the ice cream stand your sister dropped her ice cream and burst into tears. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how your sister felt when she dropped her ice cream \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(139, 'One night, I was woken up by a strange noise coming from somewhere in our flat. I got out of bed to investigate. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(140, 'You were walking through the park and saw a girl picking flowers from one of the beautiful display beds. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you saw the girl picking flowers \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(141, 'Your friend, Mei, invited you to her birthday party and, as a present, you bought her a book you knew she would like. When you got to the party, you saw that someone else had already given her the same book. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Celebrations'),
(142, 'On your way home you took a short cut down a narrow street. As you rounded the corner you came face to face with an angry-looking dog. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you saw the dog \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(143, 'Your father was driving you home one evening when the car started making a funny noise and slowing down. Suddenly, the car stopped completely. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt - what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(144, 'You had bought a DVD in a shop and were just walking out through the doors when the anti-shoplifting alarm sounded. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when the alarm went off \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(145, 'I had entered a competition to win a bike. On the day the results were to be posted on the website, my Internet access went down. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- why you entered the competition \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Technology'),
(146, 'My friends and I had arranged to go swimming. I paid my entrance fee and went in. When I got to the changing rooms I realised I had forgotten my swimming things. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you realised you had forgotten your swimming things \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may also include other relevant points. You may reorder the points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(147, 'Your father had asked you to fetch his glasses trom the car, which he parked in the street. When you tried to open the door of the car with the key, the alarm turned on and a man started shouting at you. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(148, 'We were waiting at the bus stop when suddenly a dog ran into the road. A car swerved to avoid the dog and hit another car. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when you saw the accident \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. \r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(150, 'I was in the supermarket yesterday doing some shopping for my mother. It was only when it was my turn at the checkout that I realised I had forgotten the money. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(151, 'Last weekend I offered to help my parents in the garden. They were very pleased and asked me to tidy the vegetable patch. Unfortunately, I do not know much about plants. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt when your parents asked you to tidy the vegetable patch \r\n- what you did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(152, 'Yesterday morning, I left the apartment and got into the lift as usual to go school. I pressed the button for the ground floor and the door closed,  but the lift did not move. It was stuck! \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 750 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(153, 'Yesterday evening, I was at home doing my homework. My father was not back from the office and my mother had just popped out to the supermarket, so when the phone rang I answered it. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- who the caller was \r\n- what the caller said\r\n- What happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(154, 'I sing in the school choir and had been rehearsing very hard for the school concert. However, on the morning of the concert, I woke up with a bad headache. \r\n\r\nBased on the above situation, write a composition of at least 150 words. \r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your composition: \r\n- how you felt \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(155, 'A foreign student came to Singapore to study at your school for a week as part of a student exchange programme. You volunteered to host this student at your home during his or her stay in Singapore.\r\n\r\nBased on the above scenario, write a story of at least 150 words about your experiences. \r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- where the student is from\r\n- what activities you did with the student at school and at home\r\n- how both of you felt when it was time to leave\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(156, 'Write a story based on the pictures below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- what the boy was doing out at night\r\n- what the two gangsters wanted\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(157, 'Below is a leaflet for a Children''s Day celebration organised by Fun Resorts. \r\n\r\nYou are Lance and you would like to go to the carnival with your parents and your cousin who is four years old. Your parents are unsure of whether to drive there or take a shuttle service. \r\n \r\nWrite an email to enquire more about it.\r\n \r\nYou should refer to the leaflet above.\r\n \r\nIn your email, ask about the following: \r\n - whether the games and rides at the carnival are suitable for young children \r\n - what the entrance fees for adults and children are \r\n - the frequency of the shuttle service \r\n - what the usual parking charges are  \r\n - how one can get from First Avenue to Resorts Fun \r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(158, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n \r\nFor the story, make use of the points below:\r\n- what the girl in the classroom was doing \r\n- what the girl at the door was doing \r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(159, 'My parents were out and I was studying in my room one afternoon when I heard a loud crash. I rushed out of my room immediately and saw my older brother running out of the front door.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n \r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- why your brother ran out of the house \r\n- what you did next\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(160, 'Below is an email your cousin sent about a trip to Malacca. \r\n\r\nYou and your mother are keen to go for the trip.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to your cousin enquiring about the trip.\r\n\r\nYou should refer to the email above. \r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following:\r\n- enquire about your cousin''s well being \r\n- when the trip will be\r\n- what the accommodation will be like\r\n- how you and your mother would prefer to travel to Malacca and why \r\n- what your cousin and her parents plan to do there\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.\r\n', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(161, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor the story, make use of the points below:\r\n- why the boy was on the floor \r\n- what the lady on the left was doing\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(162, 'You were getting ready for school one morning when you realised that your thumb drive was not in your bag. You needed it for class presentation that day. You and your parents tried hard to search it.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n \r\n In your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - what your parents did\r\n - what you did next\r\n - what happened in the end \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Action'),
(163, 'Below is a newspaper article.\r\n\r\nYou read about your friend performing in the ChildLove concert. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to your friend asking her more about the concert. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the newspaper article above. \r\n\r\nIn your email, ask about the following: \r\n- how your friend got involved in charity work \r\n- when your friend started preparing for the concert\r\n- what it was like performing with an international star \r\n- whether your friend will be involved in any other charity work \r\n- details about the concert"\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Report', 'Situational', ''),
(164, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor the story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what the player in midair was trying to do \r\n- what was about to happen to him\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(165, 'I was at the park when I saw a sudden movement in a bush. The leaves rustled loudly. Then stopped. Just when I was about to find out what had happened, I heard a loud screeching sound coming from the bush.\r\n\r\n Based on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n \r\n In your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - why was there a screeching sound  \r\n - what you did next \r\n - what happened in the end \r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. (Use your own paper.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(166, 'Below is a poster about being a volunteer at Save A Dog. \r\n\r\nYou would like to volunteer at Save A Dog. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to enquire about the volunteer programme. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the poster above. \r\n\r\nIn your email, ask about the following:\r\n- a specific date and time for the camp\r\n- how many hours you need to volunteer \r\n- the type of dogs at the place\r\n- whether prior experience with dogs is necessary \r\n- how to apply to be a volunteer \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(167, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor the story, make use of the points below:\r\n- what the girl squatting by the pond was doing \r\n- what the monkey was doing  \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(168, 'You were at the bus stop when you saw an elderly lady chasing a young man. Just then, the young man bumped into you and he shoved something in your hand and ran off.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the young man gave you something\r\n- what the elderly lady did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(169, 'Below is a list you have made in your planner for the coming September holiday.\r\n\r\nIt is the Friday just before the one week September holiday. Your pen-pal, Emily, in Taiwan has just started her school term. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to tell your pen-pal how you intend to spend your holiday.\r\n\r\nYou should refer to the list when writing your email. \r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following: \r\n- ask your pen-pal how she spent her school holiday \r\n- what you intend to do with your friends and why it might be hard to meet up with them \r\n- what you have to do to your room \r\n- what you have not done before \r\n- what you need to do for school \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(170, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor the story, make use of the points below: \r\n- what happened to the boy lying on the ground \r\n- what the lady did \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(171, 'You were shopping at a store when the fire alarm went off. The few people in the store started running out. You were about to leave as well when you felt someone dragging you towards the front door.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the person dragged you out of the store \r\n- what you did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(172, 'Below is a leaflet about an audition for a musical.\r\n\r\nYou came across this leaflet and decide to ask your friends, Jess and Kenneth, to go for the audition with you. Like you, both of them are also interested in performing on stage. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to both your friends giving them more information about the audition. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the leaflet when writing your email. \r\n\r\nIn your email, include the following: \r\n- what you think of the musical (e.g. fun, interesting, exciting, etc.)\r\n- when the audition will be and what is needed for it \r\n- information on what the children in the chorus are required to do \r\n- how the registration can be done\r\n- why you think your friends will be interested in the musical (e.g. attended dance and singing lessons, like to act, etc.)\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(173, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long. \r\n\r\nFor the story, make use of the points below: \r\n- why the birthday girl looked shocked \r\n- what the young boy was thinking \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(174, 'You and your father were at the supermarket when your father received a call. At first, he could not hear clearly what was being said. Then, his face turned pale and he began running out of the supermarket.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- why your father was in a rush\r\n- what you did\r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(175, 'Below is a notice on your school''s Photography Club board. \r\n\r\nYou are a member of the club. Your classmate, Richard, also a member, is absent from school. \r\n\r\nWrite an email to Richard, telling him about the reminder, and including all your teacher''s instructions. \r\n \r\n You should refer to the notice when writing your email. \r\n \r\n In your email, include the following information: \r\n - the change in date\r\n - what your teacher needed help in\r\n - how many helpers are required\r\n - the time to be in school on that day \r\n - what Richard must bring \r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(176, 'Write a composition of at least 150 words, based on the picture below. \r\n \r\n In your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - what the girl was doing \r\n - what happened to her next \r\n - what happened in the end \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(177, '\r\nBelow is a notice from a library''s notice board.\r\n\r\nYou want to be a junior librarian. You think your best friend, Juliet, will be interested too. She is not at home when you look for her there. \r\n\r\nWrite a note to Juliet, telling her about the junior librarian session and asking her whether she wants to join you. \r\n\r\nYou should refer to the notice when you are writing your note. \r\n\r\nIn your note, include the following information: \r\n- the duties of a junior librarian \r\n- where and when the session will be held \r\n- when it ends \r\n- where and when to register \r\n- how you feel about the idea \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Note', 'Situational', ''),
(178, 'The pupils of 6K had just finished a test. Their teacher, Miss Smith, was collecting the test paper when someone in class shouted, "Help, Help, Miss Smith!"\r\n\r\nWrite a composition of at least 150 words, based on the situation above. \r\n \r\n In your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - who shouted for help \r\n - what happened next\r\n - what happened in the end \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(179, '\r\nBelow is a list of English programmes. \r\n\r\nYou intend to attend one of the English workshops. \r\n\r\nWrite a postcard to your friend, Ben, telling him about your decision.\r\n\r\nYou should refer to the list when writing your postcard. \r\n\r\nIn your postcard, include the following information: \r\n- which movement the programmes are being held in conjunction with \r\n- the types of workshops available \r\n- your opinion of the workshops\r\n- which workshop you have chosen \r\n- why you think you will benefit from it \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Postcard', 'Situational', ''),
(180, 'Write a composition of at least 150 words, based on the picture below. \r\n \r\n In your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - why the boy ran into the road\r\n - how the driver of the van reacted \r\n - what happened in the end \r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(181, ' Below is a page from your weekly planner. \r\n \r\n It is now Friday evening and the end of a busy week for you. \r\n \r\n Write an email to your cousin, Samuel, telling him about the busy week you have had and your plans for the weekend. \r\n \r\nYou should refer to your weekly planner when writing your email. \r\n \r\nIn your email, include the following information: \r\n - all the subjects you had homework in \r\n - the title of the composition you had to write \r\n - why Thursday''s homework was difficult \r\n - your plans for the weekend \r\n - what special occasion is about to take place\r\n \r\n You may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(182, 'I was waking home from school one day, when I head the sound of running footsteps behind me. A man ran into me and knocked me to the ground.\r\n\r\nWrite a composition of at least 150 words, based on the situation above. \r\n \r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n - who the man was \r\n - why he was running \r\n - what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events');
INSERT INTO `astarcompo_questions` (`questionID`, `question`, `questionCategory`, `questionType`, `theme`) VALUES
(183, 'Refer to the  journal entry below.\r\n\r\nYou have set yourself target grades and drawn up a plan to improve your performance in the semestral examination.\r\n\r\nWrite an email to your best friend, Jacob, telling him about your plans to do better, and asking him whether he wants to study with you.\r\n \r\nYou should refer to the journal entry when writing your email.\r\n \r\nIn your email, include the following information:\r\n- your target grades for the semestral examination\r\n- what you plan to do in class\r\n- how you plan to improve your grades for all subjects\r\n- a request to Jacob to help you in your weakest subject\r\n- what you intend to do to keep yourself healthy and fit\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.\r\n ', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(184, 'Write a composition of at least 150 words, based on the picture below.\r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below:\r\n- what the boy was doing\r\n- how the man reacted\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Unexpected Events'),
(185, 'Refer to the notice below.\r\n \r\n You have a cousin, Heidi, who lives in Begonia Estate.\r\n \r\n Write a letter to Heidi, tellling her about the recycling project and asking her to participate.\r\n \r\nYou should refer to the notice when writing your letter. \r\n \r\nIn your letter, include the following information: \r\n- what project your school is launching\r\n- what the pupils are required to do\r\n- the days and times of collection\r\n- the objectives of the project\r\n- what your cousin can do to help you \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences. \r\n ', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(186, 'The school bell rang for recess. It was raining heavily outside as the pupils walked slowly from their classrooms to the canteen. Suddenly, there was a loud thud. Everybody turned to look.\r\n\r\nBased on the situation above, write a composition of at least 150 words.\r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below:\r\n- what caused the loud thud\r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(187, 'Below is a notice that you found in your letterbox. \r\n \r\nStephen Lee is your classmate, and you want to help him to get his wallet back. \r\n \r\nWrite an email to your friend, Karen, telling her about the lost wallet. \r\n \r\nYou should refer to the notice when writing your email.\r\n \r\nIn your email, include the following information: \r\n- where and when the wallet was lost\r\n- a description of the wallet\r\n- what important documents it contains\r\n- how to contact the owner\r\n- how your friend might be of help \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Email', 'Situational', ''),
(188, 'Write a composition of at least 150 words, based on the situation above. \r\n\r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- what the boys were doing\r\n- what was inside the box \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n ', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(189, 'Below is a page from a booklet.\r\n\r\nYou intend to enrol in one of the music classes. \r\n \r\nWrite a letter to your friend, Shirley, telling her about your plan to learn a new instrument and what decision you have made. \r\n \r\nYou should refer to the page from the booklet when writing your letter. \r\n \r\nIn your letter, include the following information: \r\n- where the music classes are held \r\n- the types of music class offered  \r\n- how some time-slots and lessons clash with your time-table\r\n- which class you have decided to choose \r\n- why you have made that choice \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You should write in complete sentences.', 'Letter', 'Situational', ''),
(190, 'It was time for recess. Nicholas opened his bag. He dug deep into the bag, looking for something, and was dismayed to find that it was missing\r\n\r\nWrite a composition of at least 150 words, based on the situation above.\r\n \r\nIn your composition, make use of the points below: \r\n- what was missing \r\n- what happened next \r\n- what happened in the end \r\n \r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points. ', 'Situation-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(191, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- what the robber demanded\r\n- how the banker cashier reacted\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(192, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- what the children were doing\r\n- whether the school bus was able to stop in time\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(193, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- what the boys saw\r\n- what the aliens did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.\r\n', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Interesting Places and Events'),
(194, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- who the boy was\r\n- why the boy was climbing over the railing\r\n- what happened to him in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(195, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- what the boy was up for stage for\r\n- why the lady in the crowd was beaming with pride\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Family'),
(196, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- how the overhead bridge collasped\r\n- whether anyone was injured in the collaspe\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(197, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- how did the burglar broke into the house\r\n- what the dog did to foil his burglary attempt\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Criminal Acts'),
(198, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nYou may make use of the following points:\r\n- how the fire started\r\n- who was inside the flat, if any\r\n- what the lady did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(199, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- why the little boy was crying\r\n- where the girl was going\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(200, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- how the girl felt when she realised the boy was cheating\r\n- what the girl did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'School and You'),
(201, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- where the mother and daughter were\r\n- what the girl saw\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(202, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- what was on the pavement\r\n- what the children did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(203, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- why the young girl was crying\r\n- what the boy did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Outdoor Activities'),
(204, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- what the other two older boys were doing\r\n- what the two younger boys were doing\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Characters'),
(205, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- what had happened to the cyclist\r\n- what the family did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters'),
(206, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- what the four girls at the bottom of the picture were doing\r\n- why the sad girl was alone\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'School and You'),
(207, 'Write a story based on the picture below. Your story should be at least 150 words long.\r\n\r\nMake use of the following points in your story:\r\n- what had happened to the old lady\r\n- what the two children walking behind the old lady did\r\n- what happened in the end\r\n\r\nYou may reorder the points. You may also include other relevant points.', 'Picture-Based', 'Continuous', 'Accidents and Disasters');
INSERT INTO `astarcompo_situationalTemplates` (`id`, `template`, `category`) VALUES
